WEBVTT

00:14.580 --> 00:18.330
<b>Huh? Young lady, you're not allowed
into the wholesale market.</b>

00:18.460 --> 00:21.830
<b>You dummy, that girl is allowed in. Watch her.</b>

00:32.420 --> 00:34.830
<b>S-she's selecting all the best stuff one after another?!</b>

00:36.670 --> 00:39.580
<b>I got some yummy-looking fish again today.</b>

00:39.830 --> 00:41.710
<b>Thank you as always!</b>

00:43.670 --> 00:45.710
<b>What a good girl!</b>

00:46.630 --> 00:49.250
<b>I see, that girl is the well-known one from the rumors!</b>

00:49.380 --> 00:52.750
<b>Right. That's Koyuzu-chan from
the Takamimi Shrine of Tsukishima.</b>

00:53.500 --> 00:57.710
<b>She's so put together, she puts adults to shame!</b>

02:31.170 --> 02:35.830
<b>EPISODE 7</b>

02:31.170 --> 02:35.830
<b>THE AROMA</b>

02:31.170 --> 02:35.830
<b>OF THE TOWN</b>

02:34.540 --> 02:35.790
<b>See ya, Koyu-chan.</b>

02:35.790 --> 02:37.460
<b>Later, Mii-chan!</b>

02:40.880 --> 02:44.130
<b>I'll bake a pie with the apples I got today!</b>

02:44.960 --> 02:50.960
<b>Koito's seemed so busy lately,
I'll put some sweet potato in it and make it a bit sweeter.</b>

02:54.170 --> 02:57.630
<b>Ah, Sis, you're home! I'm back!</b>

02:58.080 --> 02:59.710
<b>Welcome home, Koyuzu.</b>

02:59.710 --> 03:02.880
<b>Hey, I'm going to make that apple pie you love as a sna-</b>

03:03.790 --> 03:05.210
<b>Ah, gimme a minute.</b>

03:05.540 --> 03:13.080
<b>Hello, Kado-chan? I'm just about to leave.
Eh, paper cups? Got it, I'll buy some on the way.</b>

03:15.420 --> 03:17.420
<b>Are you getting ready for an event over the holidays?</b>

03:17.830 --> 03:19.540
<b>I'm just helping out.</b>

03:20.000 --> 03:22.880
<b>Gramps is busy right now, too, so I've gotta do it.</b>

03:23.080 --> 03:23.920
<b>Right.</b>

03:23.920 --> 03:27.250
<b>I'll be back late, so go ahead and eat dinner!</b>

03:29.210 --> 03:32.290
<b>I'm sorry, Koyuzu. Were you about to say something?</b>

03:32.580 --> 03:34.420
<b>Oh no, it was nothing.</b>

03:34.420 --> 03:36.540
<b>Really? Then I'm heading out!</b>

03:36.540 --> 03:38.210
<b>Okay, take care!</b>

03:41.580 --> 03:44.580
<b>THE NEXT DAY</b>

03:44.920 --> 03:51.250
<b>Takamimi-sama, oh, Takamimi-sama.</b>

03:51.540 --> 04:05.460
<b>We exist for today and tomorrow,
for after that we return to the soil of Tsukuda.</b>

04:05.460 --> 04:06.330
<b>Sis?</b>

04:07.670 --> 04:09.540
<b>Will you be home all day today?</b>

04:09.630 --> 04:13.630
<b>Yeah. Grampa went out today so I'm staying home.</b>

04:14.210 --> 04:18.460
<b>Y-you know, I got a research project from school today...</b>

04:18.790 --> 04:20.080
<b>Research project?</b>

04:22.790 --> 04:26.750
<b>"Ask your Grandpa and Grandma what kind of games
they played in the old days."</b>

04:23.460 --> 04:27.960
<b>"Ask your Grandpa and Grandma what kind</b>

04:23.460 --> 04:27.960
<b>of games they played in the old days."</b>

04:27.170 --> 04:29.170
<b>Eh? Sounds like fun.</b>

04:29.500 --> 04:32.290
<b>B-but Grandpa isn't here...</b>

04:32.290 --> 04:33.500
<b>Oh, you're right.</b>

04:34.130 --> 04:36.130
<b>I heard what you said.</b>

04:37.250 --> 04:38.750
<b>That lifeless voice must be...</b>

04:39.750 --> 04:40.670
<b>Elda!</b>

04:41.080 --> 04:44.290
<b>You can ask me if you want to know about games.</b>

04:44.630 --> 04:47.080
<b>Really?! Thanks, Elda-sama!</b>

04:47.460 --> 04:50.580
<b>Yeah! You can get answers from Elda!
She plays every day!</b>

04:50.670 --> 04:52.960
<b>I can get answers from Elda! She has fun every day!</b>

04:52.960 --> 04:56.790
<b>W-wait, I take the time to do
my rituals and prayers, though...</b>

05:00.750 --> 05:02.670
<b>Games in the olden days, huh...?</b>

05:03.580 --> 05:08.710
<b>What did the kids in the Edo period play with?
They must've played stuff like hanafuda, right?</b>

05:09.000 --> 05:13.000
<b>Hmm... hanafuda cards were kind of outlawed...</b>

05:13.710 --> 05:17.130
<b>The most popular thing to play in Edo was "ikanobori."</b>

05:17.290 --> 05:18.500
<b>Ikanobori?</b>

05:18.920 --> 05:20.250
<b>It means "takoage," or flying kites.</b>

05:20.420 --> 05:24.630
<b>In the Edo days, what we now call "flying octopus"
was called "ikanobori," or "flying squid."</b>

05:20.540 --> 05:21.830
<b>Takoage (Flying Octopus)</b>

05:22.330 --> 05:23.580
<b>Ikanobori (Flying Squid)</b>

05:24.830 --> 05:28.540
<b>Wow! Why did it go from "squid" to "octopus"?</b>

05:28.670 --> 05:38.380
<b>This is</b>

05:28.670 --> 05:38.380
<b>an octopus!</b>

05:28.670 --> 05:38.380
<b>Not a squid!</b>

05:28.880 --> 05:32.790
<b>When the shogunate banned
flying kites for being too popular,</b>

05:32.790 --> 05:38.080
<b>the children of Edo declared "This isn't a squid,
it's an octopus!" and kept doing it.</b>

05:38.540 --> 05:43.380
<b>Hearing that makes me think
you're a real old-fashioned Tokyoite, Elda!</b>

05:43.380 --> 05:44.710
<b>Oh? Why?</b>

05:45.210 --> 05:50.880
<b>I... I promised I'd have one Red Bull a day,
but this is a Monster Energy so it doesn't count!</b>

05:51.040 --> 05:52.130
<b>When you said that.</b>

05:52.130 --> 05:53.830
<b>Sh-shut your yapper...</b>

05:54.460 --> 05:59.880
<b>And, for girls like Koyuzu, big sister dolls were popular.</b>

06:00.420 --> 06:03.540
<b>Big sister? A doll of your big sister?</b>

06:03.710 --> 06:07.960
<b>A bride or a young woman were called "Big sister."</b>

06:08.420 --> 06:12.420
<b>That's because the fashion of the women in Edo
differed by age and job.</b>

06:12.920 --> 06:19.500
<b>While the girls were playing house using
the big sister dolls, they learned the latest fashions.</b>

06:20.040 --> 06:23.170
<b>I didn't know kids in the Edo era were playing house, too.</b>

06:23.630 --> 06:27.420
<b>Speaking of, I used to play house with you
way back in the day.</b>

06:27.420 --> 06:31.630
<b>Yeah, I had so much fun!
We made rice dumplings and everything.</b>

06:31.630 --> 06:36.080
<b>Oh? So there were times that even you
used mud balls to make food, Koyuzu?</b>

06:36.080 --> 06:39.960
<b>Festival Food</b>

06:36.290 --> 06:41.420
<b>Nope! When Koyuzu plays house,
she makes the real deal! And they're scrumptious!</b>

06:41.630 --> 06:44.250
<b>I-isn't that just doing chores then?</b>

06:48.330 --> 06:51.960
<b>And, when I think of games of Japan,
this is what comes to mind.</b>

06:52.250 --> 06:54.000
<b>Oh! Origami!</b>

06:54.000 --> 06:57.540
<b>In the Edo days we called it things
like "orisue" and "origata."</b>

06:55.830 --> 06:56.960
<b>Orisue</b>

06:55.830 --> 06:56.960
<b>Origata</b>

06:59.170 --> 07:00.380
<b>Here, a frog.</b>

07:00.380 --> 07:02.210
<b>Wow, cute!</b>

07:03.290 --> 07:04.670
<b>Next is a penguin.</b>

07:04.880 --> 07:08.170
<b>Amazing! Elda, you're really good at origami!</b>

07:08.170 --> 07:10.670
<b>I suppose. I've been doing it for 400 years, you know.</b>

07:11.290 --> 07:14.880
<b>Now that I think about it, there's some intricate origami
at the shrine office entrance.</b>

07:15.500 --> 07:19.330
<b>Yes, I made all of those.
I saw how to fold them on the net.</b>

07:19.330 --> 07:20.420
<b>Seriously?!</b>

07:33.420 --> 07:34.960
<b>Elda, you're so cool!</b>

07:40.420 --> 07:42.580
<b>How about it, Koyuzu? Did you get what you needed?</b>

07:42.750 --> 07:45.880
<b>Yeah! Thanks, Elda-sama, Sis!</b>

07:46.170 --> 07:50.420
<b>Whoops! It's too early to end this quite yet, young ladies.</b>

07:50.420 --> 07:52.790
<b>Hm? Do you have anything else add?</b>

07:53.080 --> 07:57.960
<b>Koyuzu, can you bring me water,
dish soap, and some sugar, please?</b>

07:57.960 --> 07:59.630
<b>Huh? Y-yeah.</b>

08:03.750 --> 08:08.880
<b>First, put 5 grams of sugar into 100 cc of water,
and completely dissolve it.</b>

08:10.460 --> 08:14.670
<b>Next, add 5 grams of soap and mix well...</b>

08:17.250 --> 08:19.130
<b>I know what it is! Soap bubbles!</b>

08:19.130 --> 08:20.380
<b>Correct!</b>

08:20.830 --> 08:26.670
<b>Whoa, you can make the mixture for soap bubbles
at home. Did the people of Edo do this, too?</b>

08:27.080 --> 08:31.420
<b>Not only did they do this,
they had expert peddlers called bubble vendors.</b>

08:29.250 --> 08:30.540
<b>Bubble Vendors</b>

08:32.040 --> 08:35.710
<b>They used thin bamboo tubes instead of straws.</b>

08:35.960 --> 08:42.080
<b>The soap was made from the skin of the fruit of a plant
called the soapberry. Now then, let's sta-</b>

08:43.630 --> 08:45.460
<b>You can't do this in your room.</b>

08:45.540 --> 08:49.580
<b>I know! Since you've done all this,
let's go to the Sumida River and send them flying!</b>

08:51.210 --> 08:53.290
<b>You two have fun doing that.</b>

08:53.750 --> 08:55.750
<b>Don't smile and send us off like that!</b>

08:55.750 --> 08:57.750
<b>You want to stay here that badly?!</b>

08:57.750 --> 09:01.130
<b>Let's... let's do some
on the shrine grounds, Elda-sama! Okay?!</b>

09:10.210 --> 09:11.210
<b>E-eh?</b>

09:11.630 --> 09:16.170
<b>Elda, you're really bad at blowing bubbles!
You gotta do it like this, watch!</b>

09:21.790 --> 09:22.790
<b>Wh-what?</b>

09:22.960 --> 09:25.080
<b>We're both pretty bad, eh?</b>

09:35.750 --> 09:38.330
<b>Wow, amazing job!</b>

09:38.330 --> 09:39.750
<b>You're so talented, Koyuzu!</b>

09:55.580 --> 09:58.880
<b>Man, they had a good time back then,
playing in the old days.</b>

09:59.500 --> 10:02.000
<b>What do you think, Koyuzu?
Can you get your homework done?</b>

10:05.960 --> 10:07.040
<b>Something wrong?</b>

10:07.290 --> 10:11.130
<b>I'm sorry... I lied.</b>

10:11.130 --> 10:11.920
<b>Huh?</b>

10:12.210 --> 10:15.170
<b>I didn't have a research project for homework.</b>

10:16.790 --> 10:18.710
<b>Then what's that handout about?</b>

10:19.000 --> 10:22.250
<b>I made it myself... using a computer.</b>

10:22.250 --> 10:25.000
<b>Th-that's some high-quality fabrication...</b>

10:28.170 --> 10:30.080
<b>Why'd you lie about this?</b>

10:31.670 --> 10:36.080
<b>You've been so busy lately and you're rarely at home...</b>

10:36.920 --> 10:41.290
<b>You have your job as a miko,
and I thought I couldn't bother you during that, but...</b>

10:42.290 --> 10:48.500
<b>I wanted to play with you again,
like we used to a long time ago. I'm sorry.</b>

10:56.750 --> 11:00.790
<b>Koyuzu... You're still not good
at getting the pampering you want, huh?</b>

11:03.380 --> 11:04.130
<b>Yeah.</b>

11:13.790 --> 11:16.750
<b>Let's go shopping together somewhere next week!</b>

11:16.750 --> 11:17.710
<b>Okay!</b>

11:25.380 --> 11:27.130
<b>Oh, it's Koyuzu-chan.</b>

11:27.250 --> 11:29.170
<b>Working hard again today, huh?</b>

11:29.750 --> 11:31.580
<b>Remarkable how she's always coming here.</b>

11:32.460 --> 11:35.630
<b>Don't you ever want to skip a day
and go play somewhere or something?</b>

11:36.960 --> 11:38.920
<b>I definitely go out and play!</b>

11:41.500 --> 11:43.460
<b>Adorable!</b>

12:02.630 --> 12:05.290
<b>Hm? Th-that's...</b>

12:05.960 --> 12:08.040
<b>Frog Tank Set 3!</b>

12:08.170 --> 12:10.880
<b>Th-they're supposed to be unavailable for purchase!</b>

12:12.130 --> 12:13.790
<b>Ah! And over there!</b>

12:14.080 --> 12:16.790
<b>Th-this one's a Frog Submarine.</b>

12:17.040 --> 12:19.670
<b>Th-that's a Ground-type Tadpolecopter...</b>

12:20.130 --> 12:24.830
<b>I-it's a Frog Ballute... I-i-i-it's Frog Impulse!</b>

12:26.540 --> 12:28.880
<b>Th-this is the fashion town, Shibuya!</b>

12:29.210 --> 12:32.630
<b>F-fashionable people are gonna make fun of my ears!</b>

12:32.630 --> 12:34.040
<b>I-I've gotta get outta here!</b>

12:34.540 --> 12:35.830
<b>H-huh?</b>

12:36.130 --> 12:38.540
<b>I-I don't know the way home!</b>

12:38.750 --> 12:46.130
<b>Koito, Koito! Help me! Koitooo!</b>

12:51.420 --> 12:53.880
<b>I-it was a dream.</b>

12:55.130 --> 12:58.420
<b>People in Shibuya will not make fun of your ears.</b>

12:58.750 --> 13:01.580
<b>You had a weird dream
because you slept under the kotatsu.</b>

13:01.580 --> 13:05.130
<b>N-no! I know the cause of my nightmare!</b>

13:05.460 --> 13:07.920
<b>Golden Frog Panzer</b>

13:08.040 --> 13:09.830
<b>Ooh, it's shiny gold.</b>

13:10.250 --> 13:15.000
<b>The ultra rare item from
the Frog Tanks Set 3 Sales Campaign!</b>

13:15.460 --> 13:19.040
<b>It was sold by lottery, but I never won.</b>

13:19.460 --> 13:24.790
<b>Gaah, I want it! I just can't believe
that the Frog Tank I like is so shiny!</b>

13:25.250 --> 13:29.040
<b>Elda, you really like sparkly, shiny things.</b>

13:29.330 --> 13:30.830
<b>Were you a crow in your previous life?</b>

13:31.380 --> 13:34.540
<b>Wait... but I feel like I've seen this one somewhere.</b>

13:34.540 --> 13:37.750
<b>R-really?! Wh-wh-wh-where?!</b>

13:37.960 --> 13:40.000
<b>Hmm... Oh, I know.</b>

13:40.540 --> 13:43.080
<b>It's a prize at the shopping arcade's raffle event.</b>

13:43.540 --> 13:47.130
<b>Th-that thing you've been helping set up for recently?</b>

13:47.130 --> 13:47.880
<b>Yup.</b>

13:48.250 --> 13:51.460
<b>Right now, Monjya Street is holding a stamp rally!</b>

13:48.380 --> 13:51.750
<b>Exiciting</b>

13:48.380 --> 13:51.750
<b>Stamp Rally</b>

13:48.380 --> 13:51.750
<b>Monjya Street</b>

13:51.920 --> 13:54.960
<b>If you shop or eat there, you get one stamp!</b>

13:55.040 --> 13:57.420
<b>When you get five stamps, you can enter the raffle!</b>

13:57.880 --> 14:02.790
<b>Top prize is an amazing trip to Hawaii!
Aloha! I'd love to go!</b>

14:03.290 --> 14:09.460
<b>A-a stamp rally? We had those in Edo, too. It was called
"Yanaka Seven Deities of Good Fortune Tour,"</b>

14:09.290 --> 14:11.130
<b>"Yanaka Seven Deities of Good Fortune Tour"</b>

14:09.460 --> 14:11.790
<b>and we'd visit shrine and temples
and collect their seal stamps.</b>

14:11.880 --> 14:18.880
<b>1</b>

14:11.880 --> 14:18.880
<b>Long Life</b>

14:11.880 --> 14:18.880
<b>and Fortune</b>

14:11.880 --> 14:18.880
<b>2</b>

14:11.880 --> 14:18.880
<b>Success</b>

14:11.880 --> 14:18.880
<b>in Business</b>

14:11.880 --> 14:18.880
<b>3</b>

14:11.880 --> 14:18.880
<b>Good</b>

14:11.880 --> 14:18.880
<b>Fortune</b>

14:11.880 --> 14:18.880
<b>4</b>

14:11.880 --> 14:18.880
<b>Long Life</b>

14:11.890 --> 14:18.880
<b>and Happiness</b>

14:11.890 --> 14:18.880
<b>5</b>

14:11.890 --> 14:18.880
<b>Victory</b>

14:11.890 --> 14:18.880
<b>6</b>

14:11.890 --> 14:18.880
<b>Rich    </b>

14:11.890 --> 14:18.880
<b>Harvest</b>

14:11.890 --> 14:18.880
<b>7</b>

14:11.890 --> 14:18.880
<b>Good Results</b>

14:11.890 --> 14:18.880
<b>in Learning</b>

14:12.130 --> 14:14.130
<b>You can ignore Hawaii,</b>

14:14.250 --> 14:18.630
<b>but have you thought about whether it's godly to call
the seal stamps from shrines and temples a stamp rally?</b>

14:18.880 --> 14:24.790
<b>F-Frog Tanks are the fifth place prize?
I-if they're fifth place, I might have a chance to win, right?!</b>

14:25.130 --> 14:28.290
<b>K-Koito, collect stamps for me!</b>

14:28.290 --> 14:31.580
<b>No way, you gotta collect them yourself. See, look.</b>

14:31.790 --> 14:34.210
<b>You can't transfer stamps to someone else.</b>

14:34.210 --> 14:36.170
<b>Huh?! Th-that's not fair!</b>

14:40.460 --> 14:43.630
<b>Does a seal stamp from Takamimi Shrine count?</b>

14:43.920 --> 14:46.880
<b>Of course not. Besides, that's a legal seal.</b>

14:47.460 --> 14:50.420
<b>Tsukishima</b>

14:47.460 --> 14:50.420
<b>Nishinaka Street First Avenue</b>

14:50.830 --> 14:56.080
<b>This may be my first time going out with you
while the sun's still up. Right, Elda?</b>

15:03.080 --> 15:05.460
<b>Do you really have to wear that?</b>

15:05.460 --> 15:10.250
<b>K-Koito, a s-street with less of a human presence
is better... Let's go down this alley!</b>

15:11.290 --> 15:13.500
<b>I can't believe this is our enshrined deity.</b>

15:16.710 --> 15:18.080
<b>It's Takamimi-sama.</b>

15:18.080 --> 15:20.080
<b>What an honor, we are blessed!</b>

15:20.830 --> 15:25.920
<b>She's incredibly obvious right now...
but they're so careful to worship her in secret.</b>

15:28.130 --> 15:29.420
<b>I could hardly breathe...</b>

15:29.670 --> 15:32.420
<b>Have you always worn
that sort of thing to go out shopping?</b>

15:32.420 --> 15:37.630
<b>N-no, in the Edo days,
street merchants would come right to your house.</b>

15:37.920 --> 15:38.920
<b>Street merchants?</b>

15:38.210 --> 15:39.420
<b>Street merchants</b>

15:39.670 --> 15:43.040
<b>They're people who would hang their goods
underneath each arm on a carrying pole,</b>

15:43.040 --> 15:46.540
<b>and walk among the row houses
and where samurai lived and sell their wares.</b>

15:46.790 --> 15:50.080
<b>I often had prepared food items
and the like delivered to me.</b>

15:50.460 --> 15:54.170
<b>Oh, so it's like pizza delivery and Uher Eats, then.</b>

15:54.170 --> 15:58.250
<b>They sold daily necessities,
and even things like goldfish and crickets.</b>

15:59.130 --> 16:04.380
<b>Since it was so convenient I used it a lot and
the street merchants made a line in front of the shrine,</b>

16:04.380 --> 16:06.330
<b>and my miko at the time was furious.</b>

16:06.880 --> 16:11.880
<b>Now you have a mountain of empty
Amazen boxes instead. Clean that up, m'kay?</b>

16:12.670 --> 16:17.670
<b>All right, where should we go first?
Elda, is there anything you want?</b>

16:17.880 --> 16:22.080
<b>Five games from Shimaden! Then I'll get 5 stamps!</b>

16:22.080 --> 16:23.380
<b>I thought you'd say that...</b>

16:23.960 --> 16:30.380
<b>But actually, I got a phone call earlier. The old lady
from Shimaden is making a hospital visit today.</b>

16:26.960 --> 16:32.170
<b>WE REGRET TO INFORM YOU</b>

16:26.960 --> 16:32.170
<b>THAT WE ARE CLOSED TODAY.</b>

16:26.960 --> 16:32.170
<b>-SHIMADEN</b>

16:30.500 --> 16:32.170
<b>Oh, really?</b>

16:32.330 --> 16:35.040
<b>Yup. She wanted to see you today.</b>

16:35.290 --> 16:38.210
<b>Hmm, well, I guess nothing can be done about that.</b>

16:38.580 --> 16:42.960
<b>Then I know what I want! A bed from IKEYA!
I want to make my room nice!</b>

16:42.960 --> 16:44.790
<b>There's no IKEYA in the shopping arcade.</b>

16:45.040 --> 16:47.880
<b>Okay, let's just stroll around for now.</b>

16:51.080 --> 16:54.040
<b>FRESH BAKED</b>

16:51.080 --> 16:54.040
<b>MELON BREAD</b>

17:03.960 --> 17:06.670
<b>Exciting</b>

17:03.960 --> 17:06.670
<b>Stamp Rally</b>

17:03.960 --> 17:06.670
<b>Monjya Street</b>

17:04.330 --> 17:06.670
<b>You've gotten quite a few stamps!</b>

17:06.920 --> 17:09.290
<b>Y-yeah! Just one more left!</b>

17:11.580 --> 17:16.380
<b>A winter daphne. Everyone is still growing those, huh?</b>

17:16.500 --> 17:18.750
<b>Yeah, because that's your flower.</b>

17:19.630 --> 17:21.750
<b>In flower language it means immortal, and indestructible.</b>

17:22.000 --> 17:25.040
<b>We get the seedlings
at our elementary school graduation.</b>

17:26.330 --> 17:27.920
<b>Smells lovely.</b>

17:28.040 --> 17:31.170
<b>Yeah, I like the smell of winter daphne, too.</b>

17:35.380 --> 17:37.540
<b>It smells like the delicious aroma of that sauce.</b>

17:37.750 --> 17:38.460
<b>Yeah...</b>

17:39.330 --> 17:42.250
<b>Let's end it with monjya!</b>

17:42.500 --> 17:45.000
<b>Closed today</b>

17:45.210 --> 17:47.290
<b>Huh? Is today their day off?</b>

17:47.580 --> 17:48.290
<b>Closed today</b>

17:49.250 --> 17:53.170
<b>Oh? What's up, Miko-sama...whoa! Takamimi-sama?!</b>

17:53.500 --> 17:54.750
<b>H-hello...</b>

17:55.460 --> 17:58.040
<b>Kado-chan, is today one of your days off?</b>

17:58.040 --> 18:00.000
<b>No, it's just...</b>

18:00.580 --> 18:05.130
<b>Eeeeey! That you, Takamimi-sama? This is new!</b>

18:06.290 --> 18:10.330
<b>Sasaki barged in here
and has been drinking since lunch time.</b>

18:10.330 --> 18:11.920
<b>A..Akane-chan...</b>

18:11.920 --> 18:14.250
<b>She's drunk like in those old comedy bits...</b>

18:14.670 --> 18:20.330
<b>She said she's stressed out.
She's a bad drunk, so I'm letting her drink alone.</b>

18:22.170 --> 18:25.250
<b>Kadoi, another beer!</b>

18:26.630 --> 18:29.080
<b>Sure, but slow down a bit.</b>

18:29.080 --> 18:31.460
<b>What's wrong? Yer so serious.</b>

18:31.710 --> 18:34.380
<b>OLD</b>

18:31.710 --> 18:34.380
<b>KADOI</b>

18:31.920 --> 18:34.170
<b>And you used to be such a little punk!</b>

18:34.380 --> 18:36.130
<b>I'm not really a punk, you know!</b>

18:36.130 --> 18:38.710
<b>Th-those two are good friends, right?</b>

18:39.080 --> 18:43.040
<b>They've been best friends since junior high,
Akane-chan and Kado-chan.</b>

18:43.170 --> 18:45.130
<b>It's just a rotten relationship we're both stuck with.</b>

18:47.000 --> 18:55.710
<b>MONBEE POPULAR MONJYA RANKING</b>

18:47.000 --> 18:55.710
<b>1ST MONBEE SPECIAL</b>

18:47.000 --> 18:55.710
<b>2ND SPICY COD ROE, CHEESE</b>

18:47.000 --> 18:55.710
<b>3RD KIMCHI STEW STYLE</b>

18:47.000 --> 18:55.710
<b>4TH PORK, MUSHROOM</b>

18:47.010 --> 18:55.710
<b>5TH PORK, KIMCHI, SQUID</b>

18:47.010 --> 18:55.710
<b>6TH CAMEM BABY</b>

18:47.010 --> 18:55.710
<b>7TH NATTO, LEEKS, AND SQUID</b>

18:47.010 --> 18:55.710
<b>8TH MIXED</b>

18:47.010 --> 18:55.710
<b>9TH OMELETTE RICE</b>

18:47.010 --> 18:55.710
<b>10TH OYSTER HOT POT STYLE</b>

18:47.380 --> 18:50.290
<b>Akane-chan, are you okay? Is work getting rough?</b>

18:50.380 --> 18:55.830
<b>Koito, you're so kind. Okay! I'll pay for you! Kadoi! Beer!</b>

18:55.830 --> 18:57.710
<b>Don't offer drinks to minors.</b>

19:01.210 --> 19:06.080
<b>Oh, so Takamimi-sama wants that uh, frog toy.</b>

19:06.080 --> 19:11.500
<b>Y-yes. I'm collecting stamps with Koito
so I can enter the raffle.</b>

19:11.920 --> 19:16.040
<b>Some freakin' raffle! I wanna go to Hawaii, too!</b>

19:16.290 --> 19:20.000
<b>Sasaki didn't win the trip to Hawaii.
She even had five chances.</b>

19:20.000 --> 19:21.710
<b>A-Akane...</b>

19:21.920 --> 19:24.170
<b>Would you like to do a purification ritual
at the shrine soon?</b>

19:24.170 --> 19:26.250
<b>Our amulets have a great reputation.</b>

19:26.500 --> 19:32.330
<b>Shuddup! I wouldn't be able to take
a vacation even if I did win!</b>

19:35.210 --> 19:35.420
<b>Exciting Stamp Rally in Monjya Street</b>

19:35.420 --> 19:37.630
<b>We got them!</b>

19:38.330 --> 19:40.130
<b>Let's get to the raffle right away!</b>

19:40.130 --> 19:42.920
<b>O-Okay...! I'm nervous now.</b>

19:44.000 --> 19:46.000
<b>Well, thanks for the meal!</b>

19:46.000 --> 19:47.250
<b>Come back again sometime.</b>

19:51.170 --> 19:53.580
<b>I got to talk with Takamimi-sama again!</b>

19:55.540 --> 19:58.670
<b>What? They left!</b>

19:58.880 --> 20:00.960
<b>They said they're going to the raffle.</b>

20:01.710 --> 20:04.880
<b>Speaking of, Sasaki, did you win anything at all?</b>

20:04.880 --> 20:08.880
<b>Hmm? Yeah, I won. Just once.</b>

20:10.960 --> 20:12.580
<b>Some weird...</b>

20:12.580 --> 20:13.830
<b>...golden...</b>

20:15.040 --> 20:16.630
<b>...frog thing.</b>

20:19.040 --> 20:22.920
<b>That's the thing Takamimi-sama wanted...</b>

20:26.250 --> 20:30.920
<b>Raffle Spot</b>

20:30.920 --> 20:35.630
<b>Tsukishima Monjya Promotional Cooperative</b>

20:31.210 --> 20:33.080
<b>It's finally happening, Koito!</b>

20:33.210 --> 20:35.000
<b>It sure is, Elda!</b>

20:36.080 --> 20:38.330
<b>I'd really like to go to Hawaii, though.</b>

20:40.670 --> 20:41.920
<b>Takamimi-sama...</b>

20:41.330 --> 20:46.290
<b>Parishioners thoughtfully watching over her from the shadows</b>

20:42.960 --> 20:44.960
<b>She collected stamps.</b>

20:45.830 --> 20:47.210
<b>Best of luck!</b>

20:48.420 --> 20:50.040
<b>We'd like a try, please!</b>

20:50.040 --> 20:53.210
<b>Okay, that's one pull. Go ahead.</b>

20:53.540 --> 20:58.630
<b>U-um, fifth place is... Fifth place is a black ball!</b>

20:59.710 --> 21:03.880
<b>K-Koito! Will you do it for me?</b>

21:03.880 --> 21:08.830
<b>Eh, why? You should do it
since you worked hard to get all those stamps.</b>

21:09.130 --> 21:14.710
<b>I still haven't recovered from the trauma
of getting three Tadpolecopters...</b>

21:15.380 --> 21:21.000
<b>Okay... in the end, you got a box full of tadpoles,
and you now have a tadpole army, huh...</b>

21:22.000 --> 21:25.790
<b>So do it for me, Koito! I only have this one chance!</b>

21:26.330 --> 21:29.580
<b>I'm betting on your limitless potential!</b>

21:30.500 --> 21:31.380
<b>Okay!</b>

21:32.130 --> 21:35.000
<b>Then I'll get it for you, with the power of my amulet!</b>

21:35.210 --> 21:37.790
<b>That golden frog p... thingybob!</b>

21:38.460 --> 21:40.000
<b>That's the one!</b>

22:01.790 --> 22:03.710
<b>It's black! It's black, Elda!</b>

22:03.710 --> 22:07.130
<b>H-hooray! Thanks, Koito!</b>

22:07.330 --> 22:09.000
<b>And we have fifth a place jackpot winner!</b>

22:07.330 --> 22:12.380
<b>Tsukishima Monjya Promotional Cooperative</b>

22:09.000 --> 22:10.790
<b>Congratulations!</b>

22:12.380 --> 22:14.830
<b>You get a Golden Frog Tank!</b>

22:16.210 --> 22:18.040
<b>W-we made it...</b>

22:19.000 --> 22:20.830
<b>Please put only the balls for fifth place in there!</b>

22:20.830 --> 22:22.040
<b>I'll even give this back!</b>

22:22.920 --> 22:25.210
<b>You could have just given it to her normally.</b>

22:25.670 --> 22:30.210
<b>What's wrong with it? She took her time
to get all those stamps. Ugh.</b>

22:30.210 --> 22:33.000
<b>I kind of like that about you.</b>

22:36.920 --> 22:40.750
<b>Ah, it's so pretty, this Golden Frog Panzer...</b>

22:40.750 --> 22:45.080
<b>I'm glad you got it!
Looks like my amulet was blessed after all, huh?</b>

22:45.250 --> 22:48.630
<b>I-I think so! I'm still just an elf, though!</b>

22:50.040 --> 22:54.210
<b>Thus, the elf was pampered by everyone yet again today.</b>
